The British, who in the ranks of the Ukrainian Armed Forces defended Mariupol, says that he is ready to surrender to the russians
The Britangarian, who is a servicemen of the Marine Brigade of the Armed Forces of Ukraine, who participates in the defense of Mariupol, told his friends and his family that they would lay down their weapons and surrender to the Russian occupiers.
Source: twitter-page Eydina Eislin, a Briton who has served in the ranks of the Armed Forces of Ukraine since 2018, the Air Force with reference to Eislin's family members and friends, Atlas News with reference to the words of Eyslin's friend, who talked to him
Literally twitter Eislin: "We received the news from him: "48 days have passed, we tried everything possible to protect Mariupol, but we do not have a choice other than being surrendered to the Russian troops.
We don't have food and munition.
"Thank you to everyone, I hope that the war will end soon."
Oizlin served in the 36th Separate Marine Brigade of the Ukrainian Armed Forces, which participates in the defensive operation of Mariupol.
BBC journalists contacted the mother of a servicewoman En Wood, and she reaffirmed that on the phone her son said that they planned to surrender.
Military Brinan Phillips was also reiterated to reporters in the last telephone conversation, Aislin said about the plans of their subdivision for surrender.
According to him, munitions and groceries ran out.
Atlas News journalists contacted his friend, who said Eisslin' unit intends to be captured by Russian units, so as not to fall without weapons and bullets into the hands of detachments of the so-called "Kadyrovites".
Also in social networks, an audio recording of a telephone conversation was disseminated, in which Eisslin allegedly speaks with his acquaintance of an American friend who plans to go to Ukraine.
In the conversation, Eisslin said that they tried to get out of the city in civilian clothes, but they did not succeed.
Earlier, the Briton said that on Instagram he was thundered by representatives of the private military company Wagner.
Euslin was a social worker in Newark-on-Trent in Nottinghamshire, but in 2015-2017 he went to take part in the fighting against terrorists of the so-called “Islamic state” in Syria.
In 2018, he formally joined the ranks of the Armed Forces and was sworn.
Eislin's friends and relatives called Johnny, and in social networks he is better known under the nominimum zakors Gundi.
